{{- define "bodyClass" -}}page-admin{{- end -}}
{{- define "mainClass" -}}main-admin{{- end -}}
{{- define "chrome" -}}{{ template "adminChrome" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "content" -}}
<div class="section-head">
  <h2>Load runs</h2>
  <p>
    Every run this machine is publishing metrics for, whoever started it.
    <strong>Stop</strong> ends the run and frees its capacity — useful for one
    somebody left pointed at a production region, or for reclaiming a machine
    that is saturated. A run started from a command line rather than from the
    console has no owner recorded, and is an administrator's to stop.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="panel table-wrap">
  <table class="grid">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>PID</th><th>Owner</th><th>Status</th><th>Active</th>
        <th>Completed</th><th>Failed</th><th>Started</th><th>Parameters</th>
        <th class="right">Actions</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody id="rows"><tr><td colspan="9" class="empty">Loading…</td></tr></tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p class="hint">
  Stopping a run is written to the audit trail with whose it was, so "who
  stopped my soak test" is answerable from both ends. The list refreshes itself
  every few seconds.
</p>

<div class="toast" id="toast" hidden></div>
{{- end -}}

{{- define "scripts" -}}
<script src="/static/js/admin.js?v={{ .Version }}" defer></script>
{{- end -}}
